From 8a8339ef5830d3854556ead35d5b2db4e9796cf6 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: Felix Krueckel <hi@felkru.com>
Date: Thu, 8 Oct 2026 16:05:13 -0700
Subject: [PATCH 47/52] SSH Warpify on the web

The host's shell runs on the user's machine, so the init line now sets the env the
desktop PTY gets (WARP_IS_LOCAL_SHELL_SESSION, WARP_USE_SSH_WRAPPER from the Warpify
setting, WARP_SSH_REUSE_CONTROL_MASTER, SSH_SOCKET_DIR) and the bootstrap's ssh wrapper
Warpifies the remote shell in-band. The SSH extension (remote server) needs local
ssh/scp processes, so the web dispatcher has remote-server support disabled; without
that, a wrapped SSH session would hold its bootstrap forever.

Co-Authored-By: Claude Opus 5.5 <noreply@anthropic.com>
